# rknpu — device tree and driver notes

This driver binds to the DT compatible **`rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core`** with a
three-core layout (NPU power domains NPUTOP/NPU1/NPU2, per-core IOMMUs, all fed
from `vdd_npu_s0`, 200–800 MHz devfreq).

No DT patch or overlay is needed. Mainline v6.18 `rk3588-base.dtsi` defines
`rknn_core_0/1/2` (`npu@fdab0000` / `fdac0000` / `fdad0000`) and
`rknn_mmu_0/1/2`, and the Rock 5B board DT (`rk3588-rock-5b-5bp-5t.dtsi`)
already sets all six to `status = "okay"` with `npu-supply`/`sram-supply`
wired to `vdd_npu_s0`.

Those nodes are the binding of mainline's own NPU driver, **Rocket**
(`drivers/accel/rocket`, `CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL_ROCKET`, Mesa userspace). Rocket and
this driver claim the same nodes, so only one may be enabled;
`board/radxa/rock5b/kernel.config` explicitly disables Rocket so `rknpu.ko`
(RKNN toolkit compatible) owns the NPU.

Runtime pairing: `librknnrt` v2.3.2 (BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRKNNRT), which this
package selects. Verify after boot:

    modinfo rknpu ; dmesg | grep -i rknpu
    ls /dev/rknpu*
    cat /sys/class/devfreq/fdab0000.npu/cur_freq
